# Dashboard conventions

Four pages share one tab bar (order fixed): Legislation (`index.html`) ·
Hearings (`hearings.html`) · Elections Happening in IL (`elections.html`) ·
Site Architecture (`architecture.html`).

## Shared elements — keep in sync across all four pages

- Tab bar markup/order + accents (`.tab-legis` blue, `.tab-hearings` gold,
  `.tab-elections` green, `.tab-arch` purple).
- Floating `.to-top` liquid-glass "Back to Top" pill (after ~400px scroll).
- `feed.xsl` processing instruction on every RSS feed (root feeds → `feed.xsl`,
  one-directory-down feeds → `../feed.xsl`).
- "New Design" switch: `data-design="new"` on `<html>`, per-page localStorage
  key `govbot-<page>-design`, skin last in that page's stylesheet
  (elections → Robinhood green, legislation → Stripe blurple, hearings → Polymarket).
- All feed dates in Central time (`America/Chicago`).

## Pipelines

- Hearings (`actions/scrape-hearings/`): ilga/wa/ma/ak direct scrapes + federal
  Regulations.gov (fallback: committed `federal_seed.json`). Emits `hearings.json`,
  `hearings.xml`, granular feeds, `participation.json`.
- Elections (`actions/scrape-elections/`): committed `elections_seed.json` structure,
  scrapers only populate candidates; official vs `potential_candidates` strictly
  separated; per-race feeds expand to one item per candidate/milestone.
- Maps (`actions/scrape-maps/`): Chicago ward/police polygons → `maps.json`.
- Taxonomy: `scripts/govbot-dashboard.yml` `tags:` must match the keyword fallback
  in `scripts/dashboard_tags.json` (tested by `scripts/test_dashboard_tags.py`).

See `CLAUDE.md` ("Pages Dashboard") and `docs/src/dashboard-guide.md` for the
full data flow before editing dashboard code.
